Not a problem. Find a few WoDig point straight down and you'll get to 
the castle. Be sure to take a blindfold in case you survive and need to 
come back up. Or use teleport control and go straight there.

> Now yes, you are all free to pull that apart and rip it to shreds.
> You've ascended, I haven't. In fact, I implore you to improve that.
> Any help is always appreciated :D

You sound terribly specific about your equipment needs. My equipment 
needs are generally 'whatever I find' plus any enchantments I can add. I 
don't think I've ever wished for an artifact. I'd put free action, 
levitation, and teleport control (if not intrinsic) much higher up any 
list than increase damage or conflict.

I think my 'shopping list' of things to get are mostly intrinsics: 
protection, resistances, plenty hit points. Clairvoyance is actually 
pretty useful too (though even more so below the castle) once you've 
exhausted divine protection as a gold sink.

My suggestions would be: avoid killing any more than you have to until 
you've gone at least down to Medusa's level and only then start trying 
to gain levels so you can look at doing the quest. I'm not saying you 
have to do protection racket levels of avoiding things, but running away 
is good as is ignoring things that are asleep and not in the way. I'll 
probably clear important levels but once I know where the quest then 
(unless looking for Ludios) I won't always map full levels down to the 
castle.

Get teleport control: from a ring or if you want a bit of a risk a 
sixpack of tinned tengu is always on my list of things to get; plus of 
course a stack of portable level teleports. Saves a lot of walking, lets 
you keep a big stash near the quest portal and is an instant escape from 
many forms of trouble.

Above all: you know what your doing, it isn't working therefore try 
something different. Flexibility is the key: adapt your game style to 
the dungeon you find.

